     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, so this order is twice that limit. 1700 mg is also not a standard tablet strength (500, 850, and 1000 mg are the common ones).\n\nFor a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, the options that fit within labeled dosing include:\n\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day, a more conservative start)\n\nIf you intended one of these, or meant a different dose, tell me which and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg TID is intentional, please confirm and I'll enter it as written, though it exceeds the labeled maximum and I'd suggest documenting the rationale in the order note."
      }
     ],
